cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software/data, please cite the associated paper (details on publication) and this archive."
title: "Canopy-imaging phenomics recovers genetic population structure in a narrow-based rice breeding panel: analysis code and derived data"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible research compendium (analysis code and derived data) for a comprehensive
  population-genomics characterisation of two genetically disjoint rice breeding panels
  (Set 1: 150 accessions, whole-genome-resequenced; Set 2: 147 accessions, 50K array) —
  structure (PCA, sNMF admixture, UMAP, DAPC, cross-method consensus), diversity and mating
  system (He/Ho/Fis, selfing rate, rarefied allelic richness, private alleles), genome history
  (ROH/F_ROH, LD-based Ne, folded SFS and Stairway Plot demography), differentiation
  (Weir-Cockerham theta with block-bootstrap CIs, Nei Gst, one- and two-level AMOVA), selection
  scans (pcadapt; Beagle-phased iHS and XP-EHH), f3 admixture tests, LD decay, a
  genomic-phenomic concordance analysis (Mantel/partial Mantel, Procrustes/PROTEST, supervised
  ancestry classification from 204 canopy-imaging features, MMRR and permutation-null
  robustness), and a diversity-maximising core collection.
